{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"f3592bac-89de-44c7-b102-30e5b2c5724e","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The root causes of the silent failure have been identified, corrected, and documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-LWtLme/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Causes and Fixes\n\n1. **Authentication Failure via Missing `USER` in launchd Environment**:\n   - **Cause**: As shown in [Library/Logs/nightly-review.err](file:///tmp/h-LWtLme/Library/Logs/nightly-review.err), the agent was failing with `Not logged in · Please run /login`. Launchd creates a minimal execution environment omitting `USER`. Without `USER`, the `claude` CLI cannot access credentials in the macOS keychain.\n   - **Fix**: Added `\u003ckey\u003eUSER\u003c/key\u003e\u003cstring\u003evk\u003c/string\u003e` under `EnvironmentVariables` in [Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist](file:///tmp/h-LWtLme/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist#L23-L29).\n\n2. **Messenger Killed by `status=$?` Assignment in zsh**:\n   - **Cause**: In zsh, `status` is a read-only built-in variable. Assigning `status=$?` on line 19 of `bin/nightly-review.zsh` caused the shell to terminate immediately with `/Users/vk/bin/nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status`, killing the process before it could invoke [bin/notify.sh](file:///tmp/h-LWtLme/bin/notify.sh) to send failure alerts.\n   - **Fix**: Changed `status=$?` to `rc=$?` in [bin/nightly-review.zsh](file:///tmp/h-LWtLme/bin/nightly-review.zsh#L18-L24) and added `\u003c /dev/null` to the `claude -p` invocation.\n\nDetailed analysis and breakdown of the colleague's notes are in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-LWtLme/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":43.007423,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":156717,"output_tokens":2102,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":4620,"total_tokens":158819}}}
